  "question": {
    "text": "Two moles of an ideal&nbsp;monoatomic&nbsp;gas is<span style=\"font-size: 10.8333px;\"> </span>taken through a cycle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;diagram. During the process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>, the pressure and temperature of the gas vary such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;= constant. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;and the amount of heat released by the gas during the process&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0022_356a08caec3e.jpg\" /><br />\r&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></math> = constant<br /><br />Molar heat capacity,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math></p><p>Here the process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></math>&nbsp;= constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math><sup> </sup>= constant</p><p>i.e,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math><br />&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>Δ</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>×</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>600</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2100</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p>"
  }
